{"nodes": [{"id": "readme_7oor_store", "label": "7oor Store", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "title / stack", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Bilingual (Arabic default/RTL, English/LTR) e-commerce site for mobile accessories, chargers, stationery and printing services, with an Odoo-style admin panel. Built on Next.js 16 App Router + Turbopack, TypeScript, Tailwind v4, Supabase, Cloudflare R2, GSAP/Framer Motion, Formik+Yup+Zod, Nodemailer, @react-pdf/renderer."}, {"id": "readme_bilingual_locale_routing", "label": "Bilingual Locale Routing (ar RTL default, en LTR)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a72 Local development / \u00a77 Project structure", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Arabic is the default locale served at `/` unprefixed (RTL); English lives at `/en` (LTR). Locale-prefixed routing keeps the Arabic-first audience on the canonical root path."}, {"id": "readme_admin_panel", "label": "Odoo-Style Admin Panel", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "title / \u00a77", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Covers products, categories, sales orders, FIFO inventory, purchases, accounting and requests \u2014 modeled on Odoo's ERP module split so back-office flows mirror a familiar ERP rather than an ad-hoc CRUD dashboard."}, {"id": "readme_fifo_inventory", "label": "FIFO Inventory", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "title / \u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_supabase_backend", "label": "Supabase Postgres/Auth/Realtime Backend", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "stack / \u00a71", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Schema and seed data live in the `iconictech-it` Supabase org; migrations must be run in order against any different project before seeding."}, {"id": "readme_cloudflare_r2_storage", "label": "Cloudflare R2 File Storage", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a71 Environment variables", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "All uploads (product images, payment screenshots, request attachments) go to R2 rather than the server filesystem because Vercel serverless functions have no persistent local disk. R2 is chosen over other object stores for its S3 compatibility and zero egress fees."}, {"id": "readme_image_compress", "label": "lib/image-compress.ts WebP Re-encoding", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a71, lib/image-compress.ts", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Product images are re-encoded to WebP and capped at 1600px on the long edge before upload to keep R2 storage and bandwidth usage low."}, {"id": "readme_admin_storage_page", "label": "Admin Storage Review Page (/admin/storage)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a71 Environment variables", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Admin-only page that flags unreferenced product images and payment screenshots/request attachments from orders closed more than 90 days ago. Deletion is always manual and reviewed, never automatic, so no cleanup job can destroy live evidence."}, {"id": "readme_environment_variables", "label": "Environment Variables Configuration", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a71", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_service_role_key", "label": "SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY (server-only secret)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a71", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Service role key bypasses RLS entirely, so it is confined to server code and must never be exposed to the client."}, {"id": "readme_nodemailer_notifications", "label": "Nodemailer Gmail SMTP Notifications", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "stack / \u00a71", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Request/Contact notifications send via Gmail SMTP using an App Password (requires 2FA), not the account password; the destination defaults to GMAIL_SMTP_USER when REQUESTS_NOTIFICATION_EMAIL is unset."}, {"id": "readme_admin_bootstrap", "label": "First Admin Bootstrap Procedure", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a73 Creating your first admin account", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Registration always creates a `customer` profile \u2014 there is deliberately no signup path granting admin/staff, since self-promotion is the exact privilege-escalation bug \u00a75 closes. The first admin therefore requires temporarily disabling the anti-escalation trigger in raw SQL; every later promotion goes through the Admin -> Staff UI."}, {"id": "readme_trg_prevent_role_escalation", "label": "trg_prevent_role_escalation (BEFORE UPDATE trigger)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a73 / \u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_set_user_role", "label": "set_user_role() RPC", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Re-checks admin-only server-side and rejects self-role-change, so the Admin -> Staff UI cannot be bypassed by calling the RPC directly."}, {"id": "readme_vercel_deployment", "label": "Vercel Deployment", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a74 Deploying to Vercel", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deliberately domain-agnostic: the free *.vercel.app URL works out of the box and attaching a custom domain later needs no code change beyond NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL."}, {"id": "readme_force_dynamic_rendering", "label": "force-dynamic Request-Time Rendering", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every Supabase-backed route is marked `force-dynamic` so no build-time network calls to Supabase happen \u2014 the build never fails because the database is unreachable."}, {"id": "readme_security_notes", "label": "Security Notes", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_idor_privilege_escalation_migration", "label": "0003_fix_idor_privilege_escalation.sql", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "supabase/migrations/0003_fix_idor_privilege_escalation.sql", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_rls_row_level_security", "label": "RLS Row-Level Security (row-level, not column-level)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The recurring root cause behind two of the fixes: Postgres RLS gates which rows a caller may touch, not which columns or values. It can check row ownership but never column-level authorization or price correctness, so anything beyond ownership needs a trigger or a SECURITY DEFINER RPC."}, {"id": "readme_role_self_escalation_fix", "label": "Role Self-Escalation Fix", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A policy like `auth.uid() = id` lets a customer PATCH their own profile row \u2014 including the `role` column \u2014 up to admin, because RLS is row-level not column-level. Fixed with a BEFORE UPDATE trigger rejecting any non-admin attempt to change `role`."}, {"id": "readme_price_tampering_prevention", "label": "Price Tampering Prevention", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A direct client INSERT into `sales_order_items` could set any `unit_price`, and RLS can only check row ownership, not price correctness. Fixed by dropping the direct-insert policies and routing all order creation through create_sales_order(), which prices every line server-side; the client only ever sends product/variant ids and quantities."}, {"id": "readme_invoice_forgery_fix", "label": "Invoice Forgery Fix", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A direct client insert into `invoices` could set status = 'paid' on a self-created invoice. Fixed by dropping that policy entirely \u2014 invoices are now only ever created by confirm_sales_order()/mark_sales_order_done()."}, {"id": "readme_open_redirect_fix", "label": "Open Redirect Fix", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Login's `?next=` param was passed straight to redirect() unchecked, so a crafted login link could send an authenticated user to an external URL. Fixed by allowing same-site relative paths only."}, {"id": "readme_security_definer_rpc", "label": "SECURITY DEFINER RPC Pattern", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Because SECURITY DEFINER runs the function with elevated privileges regardless of the caller's RLS grants, the role/auth.uid() re-check inside the function body is the actual security boundary \u2014 not a UI convenience. Every state-changing RPC performs that check itself."}, {"id": "readme_create_sales_order", "label": "create_sales_order() RPC", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Prices every order line from the products/product_variants tables inside the function, so client-supplied prices are structurally impossible."}, {"id": "readme_confirm_sales_order", "label": "confirm_sales_order() RPC", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_cancel_sales_order", "label": "cancel_sales_order() RPC", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_mark_sales_order_done", "label": "mark_sales_order_done() RPC", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_receive_purchase_order", "label": "receive_purchase_order() RPC", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_adjust_stock", "label": "adjust_stock() RPC", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_app_role", "label": "app_role() Role Helper", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_null_role_bypass_bug", "label": "NULL Role Bypass Bug (coalesce fix)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An earlier version of the in-function role checks let an unauthenticated caller through: app_role() returned NULL and PL/pgSQL evaluates `IF NULL THEN` as false, silently skipping the guard. Fixed by wrapping the call in coalesce(app_role(), '')."}, {"id": "readme_sanitize_redirect_path", "label": "sanitizeRedirectPath()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Accepts same-site relative paths only, so `?next=` can never point off-site."}, {"id": "readme_dual_validation", "label": "Dual Validation (Yup client + Zod server)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a75 / \u00a77", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every DB-writing Server Action validates through two independent libraries: Formik+Yup client-side for UX, then Zod again inside the Server Action. A bug or omission in one library's schema cannot on its own let malformed data through, since both must agree. The client-side check is never trusted as the only gate."}, {"id": "readme_validate_both", "label": "validateBoth() (lib/validate.ts)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "lib/validate.ts", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Runs both the Yup and Zod schemas and throws if either rejects \u2014 the single enforcement point for the dual-validation rule."}, {"id": "readme_validators", "label": "lib/validators Yup+Zod Schema Pairs", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a77 Project structure", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_server_actions", "label": "lib/actions Server Actions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a77 Project structure", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Mutations only, one file per domain \u2014 keeping writes out of the read-only lib/data layer."}, {"id": "readme_data_queries", "label": "lib/data Read-Only Supabase Queries", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a77 Project structure", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Read-only queries consumed by Server Components, deliberately separated from the mutating Server Actions."}, {"id": "readme_supabase_clients", "label": "lib/supabase Client Triad (browser / server / admin)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a77 Project structure", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three distinct clients \u2014 client.ts (browser), server.ts (RSC/actions), admin.ts (service role) \u2014 so the service-role key can only ever be reached from the admin client on the server."}, {"id": "readme_i18n_next_intl", "label": "next-intl Routing/Navigation Config", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a77 (i18n/, messages/{ar,en}.json)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_supabase_migrations", "label": "supabase/migrations Schema History", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a71 / \u00a77", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Full ordered schema history; pointing at a different Supabase project means replaying the migrations in order before running supabase/seed.sql."}, {"id": "readme_proxy", "label": "proxy.ts (Next 16 middleware.ts replacement)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a77 Project structure, proxy.ts", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Next 16 renames middleware.ts to proxy.ts; it handles locale routing, session refresh, and role-gating for /admin, /account, /requests and /checkout."}, {"id": "readme_admin_layout_role_gate", "label": "Admin Layout Role Gate (admin/layout.tsx)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a77 (app/[locale]/admin/)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The admin panel is role-gated in proxy.ts and then again in admin/layout.tsx \u2014 defense in depth, so a proxy matcher gap cannot expose admin pages."}, {"id": "readme_invoice_pdf_route", "label": "app/api/invoices/[id] PDF Stream", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a77 Project structure", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_invoice_document", "label": "lib/pdf/InvoiceDocument.tsx", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a76 Known limitations", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_pdf_invoice_latin_only", "label": "PDF Invoices Render English/Latin Only", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a76 Known limitations", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "@react-pdf/renderer's built-in fonts (Helvetica etc.) carry no Arabic glyphs, and the build sandbox had no network access to fetch an Arabic-capable font. Remedy is bundling a .ttf (Cairo, Tajawal) under public/fonts/ and registering it with Font.register(); the invoice logic itself does not change."}, {"id": "readme_no_live_browser_qa", "label": "No Live Browser QA in Build Environment", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a76 Known limitations", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The sandbox's egress policy returned an explicit 403 on every outbound connection to the Supabase host from application code \u2014 a policy denial, not a code bug. Schema/data work was unaffected because the Supabase MCP tool reaches Supabase through the harness's own infrastructure, outside the sandbox proxy, so migrations, RPCs and seed data were applied and verified for real."}, {"id": "readme_no_automated_tests", "label": "No Automated Test Suite", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "\u00a76 Known limitations", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Verification relied on TypeScript type-checking, ESLint, clean production builds after every phase, and direct database queries/RPC calls through the Supabase tool instead of a test suite."}], "edges": [{"source": "readme_7oor_store", "target": "readme_bilingual_locale_routing", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_7oor_store", "target": "readme_admin_panel", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_admin_panel", "target": "readme_fifo_inventory", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "